= Measure  [M-nn] =

//How a Premise or Claim would be operationalized. Documented in the Foundation so that Claims can be written testable rather than retrofitted later.//

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|Stable identifier, unique within this entity type (e.g. M-01, M-02…).
|Name|A short, human-readable label for this instance.
|Status|Not Started / In Progress / Under Review / In Evaluation / Finalized.
|Evidence basis|How this knowledge was obtained — direct observation, interview, literature, secondary data, or proxy informant — flagged as provisional where it rests on anything other than direct contact with the Stakeholder group it describes. For a Measure or Evaluation Method, cite existing use in a validation study or authoritative literature (e.g. a validated-instrument source or textbook) instead.
|Construct measured|what it actually captures.
|Type|quantitative or qualitative.
|Instrument or procedure|the scale, protocol, log, or coding scheme used.
|Scoring or coding scheme|how raw observation becomes a value — for qualitative Measures, the coding rules.
|Validity and reliability|prior evidence where it exists; state plainly where the Measure is bespoke.
|Serves|Verification, Validation, or both.
|Burden|participants, equipment, time, and the ethics load it implies.

== Graph edges ==

operationalizes → (Specification-phase) Claim / Premise; used-by → Evaluation Method.